{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "A Quiet Night at Home", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Having a Good Time", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Phrasal Verbs about Socializing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use phrasal verbs when you talk about socializing or when you are socializing. Phrasal verbs are informal verbs so they fit well into conversations about and in social situations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you add a particle (preposition) to a verb, it becomes a phrasal verb. The verb changes and has a different meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Phrasal Verb Form: <br/>verb + particle (preposition)<br/><span class=\"italic\">go</span> + <span class=\"italic\">out</span> =  leave the house<br/><span class=\"italic\">take</span> + <span class=\"italic\">over</span> = gain control of", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs can be followed by phrases explaining \u2018what?' to give further explanation, but this is not always necessary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We're just going to hang out.</span> (no explanation needed)<br/><span class=\"italic\">Let's set up a weekly lunch.</span> (more explanation needed)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have no social life! I never go out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'd like to just hang out with you and Peter at the coffee shop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He hardly ever stops by these days!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're all people who want to get ahead.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's going to take over our lives for a bit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We should set up a weekly lunch date.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have got to get out more - head out to the movies or the mall!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We'll meet up once a week and take it from there.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.</p><p>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.</p><p>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.</p>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The man <span class=\"strong\">who</span>/<span class=\"strong\">that</span> called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called. <br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">man</span> - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">The book <span class=\"strong\">which</span>/<span class=\"strong\">that</span> I lent you was my father's. </span> <br/>Which book? The book I lent you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative Connector</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of Relative Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Most of the people who were in classes with me have moved away.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who were in classes with me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We're all people who want to get ahead.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who want to get ahead\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm doing work that I love.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that I love\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you ask me, the lives that we knew are gone forever. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that we knew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to hang out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's just hang out at the coffee shop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to complain about work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to stop by", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to visit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm glad that you stopped by today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to go out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to participate in social activities", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I never go out anymore!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to get ahead", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be successful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We all want to get ahead at work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to make it official", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to establish as a rule", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's make it official - we meet on Wednesdays at 7 p.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to head out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to leave for a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's head out to the movie theater.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to meet up with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet someone to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can meet up with Peter in Boston.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to take over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gain control of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Work is taking over my life!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to take it from there", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decide what to do when the time comes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We'll meet at 7 then take it from there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Cut 10 index cards in half and write phrasal verbs on the front.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a sentence on the back with a gap for the phrasal verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Shuffle cards and put them sentence side up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say the sentence using the correct phrasal verb in the correct tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take your cards to class and mix them with another student.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take turns completing the sentences.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write sentences needing phrasal verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice completing the sentences with the correct phrasal verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use correct tenses with the phrasal verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I work with another student and complete their sentences.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn7le13ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn7le13ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Let me tell you, since I started working, I have no social life! I never go out.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Neither do I. I'm doing work that I love, but it's still demanding!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'd like to just hang out with you and Peter at the coffee shop that we practically lived in at college.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: If you ask me,  the lives that we knew are gone forever. Most of the people who were in classes with me have moved away. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter included! He hardly ever stops by these days!"}, {"image": "engenn7le13ob05re2img02.jpg", "time": "28000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: We're all people who want to get ahead. It's going to take over our lives for a bit.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I really think that having a good time is important too.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Definitely. We should set up a weekly lunch date.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think that unwinding today has been so good for us. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I totally agree. We have got to get out more - head out to the movies or the mall!"}, {"image": "engenn7le13ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "51500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It's obvious that laughing and talking are great tension relievers.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I couldn't agree more.  Doing things with people who get you is so easy and fun!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: So let's make it official. We'll meet up once a week and take it from there.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes."}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le13ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le13ob05re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about social activities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can exchange opinions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How often do you meet up with friends and do something?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Who 